    {
      "id": "A1-07-l2",
      "position": 2,
      "skill": "grammar",
      "title": "some / any + like",
      "est_minutes": 30,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown_ar": "**الأسماء المعدودة** نعدّها ولها جمع: an egg ← two eggs، a banana ← bananas.\n\n**الأسماء غير المعدودة** لا نعدّها ولا جمع لها: water, milk, rice, sugar, bread, meat. لا نقول «a water» ولا «two rices»."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "مع المعدود (جمع)",
            "مع غير المعدود"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "إثبات: some",
              "There are some eggs.",
              "There is some milk."
            ],
            [
              "نفي: any",
              "There aren't any eggs.",
              "There isn't any milk."
            ],
            [
              "سؤال: any",
              "Are there any eggs?",
              "Is there any milk?"
            ],
            [
              "طلب مهذب: some",
              "Can I have some dates?",
              "Can I have some water, please?"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown_ar": "**التعبير عن الحب:** like / don't like + اسم:\n\n- I **like** fish. / I **don't like** eggs.\n- She **likes** rice. / He **doesn't like** milk.\n- **Do you like** saltah? — Yes, I do. / No, I don't."
        },
        {
