      "title": "الطعام في اليمن",
      "est_minutes": 20,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown_ar": "اقرأ عن الأكلات اليمنية في مدن مختلفة، ثم أجب عن الأسئلة."
        },
        {
          "type": "reading",
          "text_en": "Food in Yemen is different from city to city. In Sana'a, people love saltah. It is a hot soup with meat, vegetables and a special green sauce called hulba. People eat it with bread at lunch. In Aden and Hodeidah, there is a lot of fish. People eat fish with rice or with bread from the tannour. In Hadramout, mandi is very famous. It is rice with meat or chicken. And for dessert, many families make bint al-sahn. It is bread with honey and black seeds. Yemeni people drink a lot of tea with milk and sugar. Some people don't like sugar, so they drink it without sugar.",
